          "message": {
            "text": "Real Chromium normalizes the CSSOM value: contain-intrinsic-size: 0 20px reads back as 0px 20px, so the browser assertion matches /^0(px)? 20px$/ rather than an exact string (the happy-dom unit test keeps the un-normalized 0 20px kerf actually sets). Verified locally: all 3 list browser specs pass on chromium, including the off-screen-skip check via checkVisibility({ contentVisibilityAuto: true }) (visible row true, far off-screen row false) — the engine-specific optimization the unit tests structurally cannot observe.",
            "markdown": "Real Chromium normalizes the CSSOM value: `contain-intrinsic-size: 0 20px` reads back as `0px 20px`, so the browser assertion matches `/^0(px)? 20px$/` rather than an exact string (the happy-dom unit test keeps the un-normalized `0 20px` kerf actually sets). Verified locally: all 3 list browser specs pass on chromium, including the off-screen-skip check via `checkVisibility({ contentVisibilityAuto: true })` (visible row true, far off-screen row false) — the engine-specific optimization the unit tests structurally cannot observe."
          },
